# C1-S08 / B01 / C1-S09 — Aldric Returns, the Tutorial Knight, the Aldric Decision.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1737–1828.
# Scene: the tutorial knight arena (scripts/chapter1/ch1_tutorial_knight.gd).
# The legacy flags ch1_knight_killed, ch1_knight_spared and ch1_root_purge are
# read in Chapters 1–10. Keep them.
# rhythm: clipped start bark_protect bark_stay_back bark_gate bark_human_run bark_human_elara kill
# (Aldric under the directive speaks in commands, and the kill is meant to be
# quiet. Everyone else around him still talks like a person.)

~ start
Child: Uncle Aldric! You're back! I told everyone you were coming back—
do elara_goes_still
Elara: Inside. Now. Don't stop to look.
do child_runs_inside
Kaelen: Who's Aldric? That kid knew him before I could even see a face.
Elara: Someone who should be dead. Nobody else walks like that.
do aldric_approaches
Aldric: RETURN.
Elara: Aldric. Aldric, put it down.
Aldric: RETURN.
Elara: It's me. It's Elara. Look at me, not the gate.
do aldric_visor_glitch
Aldric: El—
do directive_surge
Aldric: PROTECT. THE GATE.
do start_boss aldric

# ── Boss barks: one line each, fired by the fight, never in sequence ──────
~ bark_protect
Aldric: PROTECT.

~ bark_stay_back
Aldric: STAY BACK.

~ bark_gate
Aldric: GATE.

# Phase 4: his control loop is exposed and Root Access opens.
~ bark_root_hint
Elara: His directive's showing! Root Access — {root_access} — shut it off!

# Rare. These are the man under the directive.
~ bark_human_run
Aldric: ...Run.

~ bark_human_elara
Aldric: Elara...

# ── C1-S09: Aldric kneels; Root Access exposes his directive tree ─────────
~ decision
do aldric_kneels
do show_directive_tree
System: WARNING: PURGE MAY DAMAGE MEMORY.
? Kaelen (Internal): He's on his knees, and the directive's still running. I can see every branch of it.
- End it, now, before he gets back up and hurts someone. => kill
- Hold him down. His life isn't mine to decide, not here. => spare
- Cut the directive out, even if it takes his memory with it. => purge

~ kill
set ch1_knight_killed
do kaelen_raises_weapon
# Elara doesn't stop him.
do aldric_eye_clears
Aldric: ...Good. Before it comes back.
do kaelen_freezes
Aldric: The gate... I cannot... the gate.
do directive_returns
do kaelen_strikes
do pause 1.5
Elara: He's gone. Leave the visor down.
Kaelen: I know. I'm still holding the—
Elara: Not sorry. Do not say sorry to me until you know what it is for.
? Kaelen (Internal): My hands won't let go of it. What did I just do?
- I ended his life. => kill_owned
- He was a threat, and I stopped him. => kill_justified
- I don't know yet. I can't see it from in here. => kill_unsure

~ kill_owned
set ch1_aldric_kill_owned
Elara: ...Yes. You did. Thank you for not dressing it up.
=> after

~ kill_justified
set ch1_aldric_kill_justified
Elara: He was ours before he was a threat. He stood our night watch. You will remember that part as well.
=> after

~ kill_unsure
set ch1_aldric_kill_unsure
Elara: Then don't decide it tonight. It'll keep till morning. He isn't going anywhere now.
=> after

~ spare
set ch1_knight_spared
do aldric_restrained
Elara: He might never come back from this. You know that, don't you? That child doesn't.
Kaelen: The directive's sitting on top of him. He's still under it. I saw him, for a second, when he said your name.
Elara: Do you believe that, or do you need to?
Kaelen: Mostly I need to.
Kaelen: I wasn't going to be the one who decided he couldn't come back.
=> after

~ purge
System: PURGE MAY CAUSE MEMORY LOSS.
Elara: How much memory? Tell me how much.
Kaelen: I don't know. I can see where the directive is. I can't see where he stops.
Elara: Then that is what you say first, before you put your hands inside him.
? Kaelen (Internal): If I purge it, he might wake up not knowing her. Or anyone.
- Purge it. I'll answer for whatever it takes. => purge_confirm
- Not like this. Hold him instead, while there's still a him to hold. => spare

~ purge_confirm
set ch1_root_purge
set ch1_root_purge_used
# He lives: older scenes read "Aldric alive" as ch1_knight_spared.
set ch1_knight_spared
do root_purge aldric
do pause 2.0
Aldric: ...Elara.
# She nearly laughs and nearly cries, and manages both badly.
Elara: You look terrible. You look absolutely terrible.
Aldric: You always were a liar.
=> after

~ after
set ch1_tutorial_knight_defeated
do open_shrine_gate

# Later, if he was purged and remembers enough to talk (Chapter 1 epilogue or after).
~ purged_later
Aldric: It worked on me. I am boring again. I had earned that.
Kaelen: Mostly. There are gaps I can't see the edges of. If you'd let me look again, I could—
Aldric: No. Do not make me your argument. I am a man, not a proof.
